%% DM26-0670

%% An agent asks for its signed documents each time it registers, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/signed-configuration.md, docs/architecture/soft-state.md,
%% polar-scheduler/observer/tests/replay.rs). Seen on u7s the same day: documents applied at each restart, and refused as stale when the same version came again.
%% The first delivery of a document is general/signed_configuration_delivery.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Config as ConfigurationActor<br/>(in the agent)
    participant Infra as InfrastructureSupervisor<br/>(in the agent)
    participant Cassini
    participant Obs as Scheduler observer<br/>(supervisor)
    participant Watch as GitWatcherActor
    participant Proc as Scheduler processor
    participant Graph as Neo4j

    Note over Config: Started from the render's<br/>environment. Nothing signed yet,<br/>every version at zero
    Cassini-->>Infra: Registered, at the first start and at each reconnect
    Infra-)Cassini: polar-configuration-replay { agent }
    Note over Infra,Cassini: Anyone may ask. What comes back is only what<br/>the agent would be sent anyway, signed,<br/>and idempotent by version
    Cassini-)Obs: the request. It waits on the topic for up to 180 s for a subscriber,<br/>after which it is lost until the agent's next registration
    alt the observer has not registered yet
        Obs->>Obs: keep the name (waiting_replays)
    else
        Obs->>Watch: Replay { agent }
    end
    alt the initial scan has not finished
        Note over Watch: The documents it holds are<br/>not yet the repository's word
        Watch->>Watch: keep the name, and answer once when the scan has finished
    else
        Watch->>Watch: the documents for this agent, from what it read of the checkout,<br/>by section, oldest version first
        loop each document
            Watch-)Cassini: ConfigurationNotification on agent.NAME.configuration
            Cassini-)Infra: the document, as it was read
            Infra->>Config: Deliver(document)
            Config->>Config: verify it like any other
            alt the version is above the one in force
                Config->>Config: apply, or replace the runtime section
                Config-)Infra: ConfigChanged or RuntimeChanged, for whoever follows it
            else it is the version in force, after a reconnect
                Config->>Config: refused as stale, and nothing changes
            end
            Infra-)Cassini: ConfigurationOutcome on polar-configuration-outcome
            Cassini-)Proc: the outcome, with who the broker says published it
            Proc->>Graph: one more outcome node, linked to the item it names
        end
    end
    Note over Watch,Graph: Replay goes from the observer straight to the agent,<br/>so the processor writes no new Configuration node,<br/>only the outcomes
